cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use synthbench, the reference sets or the derived metrics, please cite it as below."
title: "synthbench: a makeability benchmark for synthesizability scores"
abstract: >-
  Synthesizability scores gate most generative and virtual-screening workflows,
  and are evaluated against negative sets of computer-enumerated molecules that
  no chemist has attempted. synthbench evaluates any scorer against six
  reference sets whose makeability is known from provenance rather than from a
  score, spanning purchasable compounds, make-on-demand compounds of stated step
  count, a library demonstrated experimentally to be one aza-Diels-Alder step
  from commercial building blocks, bioactive compounds of unknown route length,
  fragment recombination products never made, and enumerated strained cages. It
  reports four quantities: makeability AUC with per-set weighting, dependence on
  the easy negative class, a hard-case comparison between one-step and never-made
  molecules, and the margin over a nearest-neighbour similarity baseline. On
  these sets that trivial baseline reaches AUC 0.785 and outperforms SAscore
  0.691, SCScore 0.352, RAscore 0.647 and BR-SAScore 0.706; removing a single
  easy negative class moves every published score below chance; and on the
  57-molecule subset confirmed by synthesis and assay every method is inverted.
  The benchmark is diagnostic and supplies no improved score.
authors:
  - family-names: "Tiwari"
    given-names: "Harshita"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/harshuharshu/synthbench"
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - synthesizability
  - synthetic accessibility
  - retrosynthesis
  - benchmark
  - de novo design
